{{Quote|Harvest is when I need you the most. It's only one season more. This year we'll make enough on the harvest that I'll be able to hire some more hands. And then you can go to the Academy next year. You must understand I need you here, Luke.''"<br />"''But it's a whole 'nother year.''"<br />"''Look, it's only one more season."''<br />"''Yeah, that's what you said when Biggs and Tank left.|[[Owen Lars]] and Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
'''Janek Sunber''',<ref name="BuildXwing German">{{BuildXWingCite|1|Starfighter Aces}} {{C|German version}}</ref> nicknamed "'''Tank'''," was an acquaintance of [[Luke Skywalker]] while living on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> Sometime during their adolescence, Skywalker, [[Biggs Darklighter]], Sunber and some of their other friends [[Mission to Beggar's Canyon|explored]] [[Beggar's Canyon]].<ref name="Announcement" /> Sometime later before the [[Battle of Yavin]], Tank joined the [[Galactic Empire]] and trained as a [[pilot]] at the [[Imperial Academy]], alongside Biggs Darklighter.<ref name="BuildXwing1" /> Sunber shared their name with the company [[Sunber Containers]].<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
"Tank" was first mentioned in the original [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], written by [[George Lucas]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> He then first appeared as the character [[Janek Sunber/Legends|Janek Sunber]] in the [[2004]] [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] [[Empire 16|''Empire'' 16]] written by [[Randy Stradley|Welles Hartley]] and illustrated by [[Davidé Fabbri]]<ref name="Empire6">[[Empire 6|''Empire'' 6]]</ref> before being identified as Tank in [[Empire 36|''Empire'' 36]] [[2005|the following year]].<ref name="Empire36">[[Empire 36|''Empire'' 36]]</ref> In the current [[canon]] continuity, Tank was first identified as Janek Sunber in the German release of the magazine [[Star Wars: Build Your Own X-Wing 1|''Star Wars: Build Your Own X-Wing'' 1]],<ref name="BuildXwing German" /> and was first pictured on the cover for the upcoming graphic novel ''[[Tales from the Outer Rim: The Legend of Beggar's Canyon]]'' set to release on [[October 13]], [[2026]],<ref name="Announcement" /> the character on the cover was confirmed to be Tank through concept art from the comic's artist [[Brent Schoonover]].<ref name="Bluesky">{{Bluesky|brentschoonover.bsky.social|post/3mddgs423p22k|[[Brent Schoonover]]|date=2026-01-26|quote=Hey everyone! Excited to announce my latest comic book project. #StarWars - Tales From The Outer Rim: The Legend of Begger’s Canyon. Written by Greg Pak with art by myself. Coming October 13th, 2026 from @madcavestudios.com under their Papercutz imprint. www.starwars.com/news/mad-cave-comics-announce|archiveurl=https://archive.is/0ws27}}</ref>

